<title>GERMANY: Good chances Germany can qualify for EMU - Tietmeyer.</title>
<headline>Good chances Germany can qualify for EMU - Tietmeyer.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Wednesday that Germany had good chances of making the grade for European monetary union this year.</p>
<p>Asked if Germany would meet the criteria set by the Maastricht treaty, Tietmeyer said: &quot;We will have to wait and see. I hope so. The chances are good.&quot;</p>
<p>Speaking to reporters before delivering a speech, Tietmeyer declined to to comment on the recent rally in the U.S. dollar against the German mark.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
